      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The displayed calculation asserts '(Q^{\\mathsf T}\\rho_0)(-Dh_0(y),1)/\\sqrt{1+|Dh_0(y)|^2}=(Q\\rho_0)(Dh(y),1)/\\sqrt{1+|Dh(y)|^2}'. Negating h changes Dh_0 to -Dh but does not change Q^{\\mathsf T} to Q. For a concrete admitted configuration, take Ω=B_3(0), D_1=B_1(0), Q=((0,0,1),(0,1,0),(-1,0,0)), and the sphere chart R(x)=Qx at x=(-1,0,0), where h(y)=sqrt(1-|y|^2) and Dh(0)=0. With ρ_0=diag(1,1,-1), the left expression is Q^{\\mathsf T}ρ_0 e_3=(1,0,0), while the middle expression is Qρ_0 e_3=(-1,0,0). Thus the written equality is false. The final normal formula is correct, but the intervening computation must retain Q^{\\mathsf T}.",
